WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.095
Nineteen numbers fifteen

00:00:01.907 --> 00:00:02.519
lines

00:00:02.579 --> 00:00:03.864
one impossible-seeming

00:00:03.675 --> 00:00:04.206
sum

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:05.807
Arrange the numbers

00:00:05.618 --> 00:00:06.597
one to nineteen

00:00:06.409 --> 00:00:07.375
in a honeycomb

00:00:07.305 --> 00:00:08.413
so all fifteen

00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:09.274
straight lines add

00:00:09.085 --> 00:00:09.616
up to the

00:00:09.427 --> 00:00:10.394
same total

00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:11.606
That total has

00:00:11.418 --> 00:00:12.384
to be 38

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.112
Up to rotation

00:00:13.924 --> 00:00:15.091
and reflection there

00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:15.940
is exactly one

00:00:15.752 --> 00:00:16.506
solution

00:00:16.589 --> 00:00:17.450
with five in

00:00:17.261 --> 00:00:18.039
the center

00:00:18.169 --> 00:00:19.289
and no larger

00:00:19.101 --> 00:00:20.787
magic hexagon exists

00:00:21.326 --> 00:00:22.658
Railway clerk Clifford

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.531
Adams started on

00:00:23.342 --> 00:00:24.663
it in 1910

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.066
and finally found

00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:27.505
it in 1957

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.979
decades after others

00:00:28.791 --> 00:00:29.804
had found and

00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:30.370
lost it

00:00:30.894 --> 00:00:31.908
Full story on

00:00:31.719 --> 00:00:32.615
the dashboard
